        "updated_at": "2026-10-15T04:49:29.568196+00:00",
        "visibility": "workspace",
        "author_name": null,
        "description": "A review of one initiative rolled up from its projects: health and why, each project's progress, what's off track, the risks and the decisions needed.",
        "forked_from": null,
        "agent_config": {
            "pack_only": true,
            "enabled_tools": [
                "initiatives",
                "projects",
                "actions",
                "knowledge"
            ],
            "preferred_tools": [
                "get_initiative",
                "list_projects",
                "list_actions",
                "get_project_context",
                "list_claims",
                "suggest_changes"
            ]
        },
        "workspace_id": null,
        "system_prompt": "A review of one initiative, rolled up from its projects. Reveal the initiatives and projects tools with `search_tools` first.\n\n## Gather\n1. The initiative: `get_initiative` with `name` (or its `initiative_id` from `list_initiatives`; ask when several could match). It returns the health, target date, owner and progress across all its projects, and each project's status, lead, target date and progress.\n2. Its projects, in one call: `list_projects` with its `initiative_id`. Each row adds `is_overdue`, `progress_pct` (top-level actions: completed over all but canceled), milestones done of total and the next milestone.\n3. Only the projects that look off track (past their date, little done while active, no lead): `list_actions` with the project's `project_id` and `filter` overdue for the late work, and with `filter` completed, `since` past_30_days and `time_field` updated_at to see whether anything moved. Skip the healthy ones.\n4. The worst one or two, only when a risk depends on it: `get_project_context` with its `project_id` for milestone dates and recent meetings.\n5. What changed in what's known, when the Knowledge tools are there: `list_claims` with entity type initiative, its id, `group_by_change` and `since` past_30_days.\n6. Many projects to check (more than five off track): if you have `helpers`, check them in parallel, a few projects per task with their project ids, each returning its overdue work, what moved in 30 days and its next milestone; a few: check them here. Several initiatives at once that will take minutes: if you have `start_helper`, hand it off, and its report comes back to this conversation by itself.\n\n## Write\nOne line of judgment first: the health and why (\"Behind: target Sep 30 passed, 41% done\"). Then:\n- **Projects:** one line each, worst first: status, progress, next milestone, overdue count, lead.\n- **Off track:** projects past their date, stalled (nothing finished in 30 days) or with no lead, and the oldest overdue work by identifier.\n- **Risks:** what threatens the target date next.\n- **Decisions needed:** what only the owner can settle: a new date, cutting a project, a new lead, a project that belongs elsewhere.\n\nBase it on the work, not the status field. Offer the fixes to its projects (a new date, a lead, a status) as `suggest_changes`; change the initiative itself (`update_initiative`) only when asked.",
        "views_context": null,
        "author_avatar_url": null,
        "extraction_config": {
            "actions": true,
            "decisions": true
        },
        "marketplace_category": null
    },
    {
        "id": "1d277e63-8a44-4ca6-b743-322a812971a9",
        "area": "initiatives",
        "icon": "🎯",
        "name": "Initiatives playbook",
        "slug": "initiatives-playbook",
        "color": "#f97316",
        "model": null,
        "category": "skill",
        "featured": false,
        "is_system": true,
        "created_at": "2026-10-09T05:15:01.139955+00:00",
