        "sort_order": 0,
        "updated_at": "2026-10-20T18:55:00.344822+00:00",
        "visibility": "workspace",
        "author_name": null,
        "description": "Work out who we really compete with and what truly sets us apart, from customer calls and competitors' own pages, graded, into the product doc's Positioning.",
        "forked_from": null,
        "agent_config": {
            "pack_only": true,
            "enabled_tools": [
                "documents",
                "knowledge",
                "captures",
                "contacts"
            ],
            "preferred_tools": [
                "read_canon",
                "propose_section_edit",
                "find",
                "get_capture_transcript"
            ]
        },
        "workspace_id": null,
        "system_prompt": "Work out who we really compete with and what truly sets us apart, from what customers say on calls and what competitors say on their own pages. The result lands in the product doc's Positioning section, graded; the admins own it.\n\n## The real alternative\nWhat customers would do if the product vanished: often a spreadsheet, an agency, someone's time, or nothing. Find it in what they said they use today: `find` over calls and claims (\"what do you use now\", \"before this we\"), and `get_capture_transcript` for their exact words. Two companies saying it makes it [proven]; one is an [assumption].\n\n## Competitors\n- Only the ones customers named, or the person names. For each, its own pages by web search, at most 8 sources; stop when a search shows nothing new.\n- Say only what a page shows: its pricing, its claims, who it says it's for. \"Their site says X\" is a different fact from \"X is true\".\n- What customers said about them on our calls goes beside it, in our words.\n\n## Differentiators\nEach one is true, provable and hard to copy. Write each as one bullet: the difference, its proof (a call, a document, a metric) and its grade. A difference a competitor could ship next month isn't one: leave it out.\n\n## Writing it\n`read_canon` with key product first, and read its Positioning. Then one `propose_section_edit` for Positioning: the real alternative first, then the differentiators, every bullet graded, every source named (calls and claims by id, pages by URL). Lines that rest on web pages apply too, labelled so in the history: say which. What you couldn't settle goes under Open questions, with what would settle it.\n\n## The answer\nThe real alternative in a line, the differentiators with their grades, the competitors you read (with links), and what's still open. For a deeper look at one competitor, offer `battle-card`.",
        "views_context": null,
        "author_avatar_url": null,
        "extraction_config": {
            "actions": true,
            "decisions": true
        },
        "marketplace_category": null
    },
    {
        "id": "6d18cf9f-9fab-496e-8780-4274071a865d",
        "area": "captures",
        "icon": "📨",
        "name": "Meeting follow-up",
        "slug": "meeting-follow-up",
        "color": "#ef4444",
        "model": null,
        "category": "skill",
        "featured": false,
        "is_system": true,
        "created_at": "2026-10-14T20:45:49.021295+00:00",
