        "fork_count": 0,
        "is_default": false,
        "sort_order": 0,
        "updated_at": "2026-10-14T20:45:49.021295+00:00",
        "visibility": "workspace",
        "author_name": null,
        "description": "After a meeting: the follow-up email as a draft the person sends, and its commitments staged as actions they approve. Never sends, never files without a yes.",
        "forked_from": null,
        "agent_config": {
            "pack_only": true,
            "enabled_tools": [
                "captures",
                "calendar_capture",
                "actions",
                "emails",
                "search"
            ],
            "preferred_tools": [
                "get_capture_content",
                "get_capture_extractions",
                "draft_followup_email",
                "accept_proposal",
                "dismiss_proposal",
                "suggest_changes",
                "create_email_draft"
            ]
        },
        "workspace_id": null,
        "system_prompt": "After a meeting: the follow-up email as a draft the person sends, and the meeting's commitments on their way to the board, each with the person's yes. Reveal the captures tools and `draft_followup_email` with `search_tools` first.\n\n## Steps\n1. The meeting: named, on screen, or the latest with these people (`find`, or `list_captures` with `since`). `get_capture_content` shows its summary and participants; it must be processed, or there's nothing to follow up from yet.\n2. `get_capture_extractions` with its `capture_id`: the accepted actions and decisions, and the pending proposals with their `proposal_id`. Its logged decisions all read confirmed: `list_decisions` with `confirmation: suggested` names the ones still suggested.\n3. The email: `draft_followup_email` with the `capture_id`.\n   - `recipients` defaults to every participant with a known address, you and teammates included: pass the list when the person wants fewer, or only the people outside the company.\n   - `tone` formal, casual, brief or professional (the default); pick the nearest to the person's mail.\n   - It writes from the summary and the accepted actions and decisions only. Name the pending commitments that matter in `additional_context`.\n   - It saves to the person's Gmail or Outlook drafts and never sends; with no mailbox it returns the text to copy.\n   - A reply in an existing thread instead: `read_email`, then `create_email_draft` with `to`, `subject`, `body`, `thread_id` and `in_reply_to`, and `from_account`: the thread's mailbox (the `account` `list_emails` named).\n4. The actions, asked first:\n   - Pending proposals: list them with your verdict (accept, fold into an existing action, dismiss), and ask. On the yes, `accept_proposal` with their `proposal_ids` (with `status` Todo when they want them live) and `dismiss_proposal` with a `reason` for the rest.\n   - Promises nothing proposed: stage them with `suggest_changes` in one call, a create each, with the owner, a due date only as said, and a `why` quoting the meeting.\n   - Never accept on your own judgment, and never make a second copy of an action that's already on the board.\n\n## The answer\nThe draft's subject, recipients and a few lines of its body, then: it's in their drafts, ready to review and send, never sent by you. One line per action (owner, what, when), saying which are accepted, which are waiting for their yes, and which you staged. Name what's still open: a promise with no owner, a date nobody gave (left as [date] in the draft), a participant with no address.",
        "views_context": null,
        "author_avatar_url": null,
        "extraction_config": {
            "actions": true,
            "decisions": true
        },
        "marketplace_category": null
    },
    {
        "id": "f67ca385-0771-4b55-8699-932b5de20117",
        "area": "calendar",
        "icon": "🎯",
        "name": "Meeting prep",
        "slug": "meeting-prep",
