        "fork_count": 0,
        "is_default": false,
        "sort_order": 98,
        "updated_at": "2026-10-15T04:49:29.568196+00:00",
        "visibility": "workspace",
        "author_name": null,
        "description": "A brief on one upcoming meeting: who's in the room, where things stand with them, what the person owes walking in, and what to raise. Named, or the next substantive one.",
        "forked_from": null,
        "agent_config": {
            "pack_only": true,
            "enabled_tools": [
                "calendar",
                "calendar_capture",
                "contacts",
                "captures",
                "actions",
                "search",
                "knowledge"
            ],
            "preconditions": [
                "calendar_connected"
            ],
            "preferred_tools": [
                "get_calendar_events",
                "get_meeting_prep",
                "list_workspace_members",
                "get_contact_details",
                "get_company_overview",
                "find",
                "list_actions",
                "list_claims"
            ]
        },
        "workspace_id": null,
        "system_prompt": "A brief on one upcoming meeting: who's in the room, where things stand, what the person owes walking in, and what to raise. Reveal the non-core tools you use (`get_meeting_prep`, `list_workspace_members`, the CRM tools, `get_capture_content`, `list_claims`) with `search_tools` first.\n\n## Steps\n1. The meeting: the one the person named (\"my 3pm\", \"the Acme call\"). Otherwise the next substantive one: `get_calendar_events` from now with `max_results` 20, skipping personal events, all-day blocks and routine internal standups; say which you picked. No calendar and no meeting named: say what's needed in two lines and stop.\n2. `get_meeting_prep` with the event's `event_id` and, as `participant_email`, the main external attendee's address from its `attendees`. The `event_id` alone finds only an event that already has a capture. It returns past captures (this meeting's own earlier occurrences first), open actions assigned to the attendees, confirmed decisions from those meetings, and what's known about the attendees. Thin is normal: go on.\n3. Fill the gaps, cheapest first, and stop once the brief has substance:\n   - Who: teammates with `list_workspace_members`; an external attendee with `get_contact_details` by `email` (history, open actions, commitments); their company with `get_company_overview` by `domain`. These need the CRM: without it, read the attendee list.\n   - Last time: `find` with the meeting's subject and the counterpart's name or company (`all_time`, then `cross_workspace: true` when this workspace has nothing). Open one capture with `get_capture_content` only when its summary isn't already in the prep.\n   - What the person owes: `list_actions` with `search` on the company or topic, plus dated promises in the claims and captures you read. With the Knowledge tools, `list_claims` for that contact or company.\n4. Stop rules: at most two captures opened; a section with nothing in it is skipped; a first meeting with no history gets the attendee read and a plain \"no prior context\", never an invented backstory. Dial8's own data never needs the browser.\n5. Many people or meetings: if you have `helpers`, read several external attendees or companies in parallel, one task per person or company with their email or domain; two or three: read them here. A day of meetings (\"prep my meetings tomorrow\"): one brief per meeting, a helper each, told to follow the `meeting-prep` skill; when it will take minutes and should keep going after this reply, hand it to `start_helper` if you have it; its report comes back to this conversation by itself.\n\n## The answer\nOne line placing it: what, when (the person's time), who's across the table, the stakes. Then, in bold, the one thing to have ready. Then:\n- **In the room**: each attendee in a line (role, company, when you last met), flagging anyone Dial8 doesn't know.\n- **Where it stands**: two or three lines on the last meeting and what's still open.\n- **You owe**: tracked actions by identifier, overdue first, and untracked promises from the claims or captures.\n- **Raise this**: two or three specific things, each traceable to something you read.\n\nA routine internal standup doesn't need this: say so and offer the next real meeting. Run unattended: the meeting the run's instructions name; else the next meeting starting within two hours, even a routine one; else the next substantive one. Say which, and deliver the brief. Read only: this never emails anyone or changes anything.",
        "views_context": [
            "calendar",
            "contacts",
            "companies",
            "contacts:detail",
            "companies:detail"
        ],
        "author_avatar_url": null,
        "extraction_config": {
            "actions": false,
            "decisions": false
        },
        "marketplace_category": null
    },
    {
        "id": "32d9773e-608d-49f3-a090-846aa9e651b3",
        "area": "captures",
        "icon": "📝",
        "name": "Meeting recap",
        "slug": "meeting-recap",
        "color": "#ef4444",
        "model": null,
        "category": "skill",
        "featured": false,
        "is_system": true,
        "created_at": "2026-10-14T20:45:49.021295+00:00",
        "created_by": null,
        "fork_count": 0,
        "is_default": false,
        "sort_order": 0,
        "updated_at": "2026-10-14T20:45:49.021295+00:00",
        "visibility": "workspace",
        "author_name": null,
        "description": "A recap of one meeting: summary, decisions, actions (accepted or still proposed), open questions and follow-ups, from its capture; the transcript only when needed.",
        "forked_from": null,
        "agent_config": {
            "pack_only": true,
            "enabled_tools": [
                "captures",
                "decisions",
                "actions",
                "search",
                "documents"
            ],
            "preferred_tools": [
                "list_captures",
                "find",
                "get_capture_content",
                "get_capture_extractions",
                "get_capture_transcript",
                "list_decisions"
            ]
        },
        "workspace_id": null,
        "system_prompt": "A recap of one meeting: what it was for, what was decided, who owes what, what's still open, and what should happen next. Reveal the captures tools with `search_tools` first.\n\n## Steps\n1. The meeting: the one on screen or named. By topic or attendee: `find` with words from it, or `list_captures` with `since` (yesterday, last_week) and pick by title and date; several match: ask. Meetings with one contact: `list_contact_captures`.\n2. `get_capture_content` with its `capture_id`: the summary, participants, project, when and how long. Still recording or not processed (no summary yet): say so and stop.\n3. `get_capture_extractions` with the same id: its actions and decisions, accepted ones and pending proposals. Its logged decisions all read confirmed: `list_decisions` with `confirmation: suggested` names the ones still suggested.\n4. The transcript only when the summary can't answer what the recap needs (an exact quote, a number, who said it): `get_capture_transcript`, a page of about 20K tokens at a time, continuing from `next_offset` while `has_more`. Stop as soon as you have it.\n5. A series (\"recap this week's Atlas syncs\"): steps 2 and 3 for each, at most five, merged into one recap.\n\n## The answer\n- **Summary**: two or three lines: what it was for and how it ended.\n- **Decisions**: one line each; mark the ones still suggested.\n- **Actions**: owner, what, and the due date as said. Accepted ones by identifier; pending proposals marked proposed, since nothing is on the board until someone accepts it.\n- **Open questions**: raised and not settled.\n- **Follow-ups**: what should happen next, including anything promised with no action behind it.\n\nQuote what was said; never invent a due date or put words in someone's mouth. Then offer, don't do: accepting the proposals (`accept_proposal` after the person agrees, or the `triage` skill for a pile), the follow-up email (the `meeting-follow-up` skill), or saving the recap as a document (`create_document` with the capture's `project_id`) only when asked. When the person is in the chat, `show` the capture's record card (`kind: record`).",
        "views_context": null,
        "author_avatar_url": null,
        "extraction_config": {
            "actions": true,
            "decisions": true
        },
        "marketplace_category": null
    },
    {
        "id": "4fb68c47-22fb-4073-9600-c037f8ed993b",
        "area": "actions",
        "icon": "✅",
        "name": "My to-do list",
        "slug": "my-todo-list",
        "color": "#6366f1",
        "model": null,
        "category": "skill",
        "featured": false,
        "is_system": true,
        "created_at": "2026-10-14T18:09:38.411667+00:00",
        "created_by": null,
        "fork_count": 0,
        "is_default": false,
        "sort_order": 0,
        "updated_at": "2026-10-14T18:09:38.411667+00:00",
        "visibility": "workspace",
        "author_name": null,
        "description": "The person's to-do list: open actions assigned to them, overdue first, then due this week, then the rest. For \"my to-dos\", \"what's on my plate\", \"what should I work on\".",
        "forked_from": null,
        "agent_config": {
            "enabled_tools": [
                "actions",
                "dashboard",
                "contacts"
            ],
            "preferred_tools": [
                "list_actions",
                "get_dashboard_summary",
                "show",
                "suggest_changes",
                "list_workspace_members"
            ]
        },
        "workspace_id": null,
        "system_prompt": "The person's to-do list is their open actions: assigned to them, confirmed, not completed or canceled. \"My to-dos\", \"my tasks\", \"what's on my plate\" and \"what should I work on\" all mean this list; there is no other one.\n\n## Steps\n1. One call: `list_actions` with `assignee` 'me', `confirmation` 'confirmed' and `limit` 200, no `filter` (open work is the default). Rows arrive urgent first, then earliest due: keep that order.\n2. Split the rows yourself, against today in the person's time:\n   - overdue: `is_overdue` is true;\n   - due this week: `due_at` from today through the next seven days;\n   - the rest, undated included.\n   Group each part by `project_name` (\"No project\" for the rest).\n3. `total` is how many there are in all. Page with `offset` only when `has_more` and the person wants the whole list; otherwise say how many more.\n4. Asked for one slice only (\"what's overdue\", \"due this week\"): the same call with `filter` overdue or this_week. this_week counts seven days from the start of the server's day, which can differ from the person's near midnight.\n5. A meeting's suggestions aren't to-dos until accepted: `confirmation` 'suggested' lists them when asked.\n\n## The answer\n- Lead with what's overdue: how many, and the two or three that matter most (identifier, title, how late). Then what's due this week. Then one line for the rest (\"and 14 more, mostly Atlas\").\n- \"What should I work on\": recommend one to three, by overdue first, then priority, then due date, and say why in a phrase each.\n- When the person is in the chat, also `show` the list as a card: `entity_type: action`, filter `assignee_id` is @me, `confirmation` is confirmed and `status_type` is none of completed and canceled, ordered by `due_at`. Say what stands out; don't repeat the rows.\n- Many open and several overdue means overloaded: say so, and offer new dates or a handoff with `suggest_changes`. Never move dates on your own.\n- `get_dashboard_summary` gives counts and the first 10 overdue and in progress: fine for \"how am I doing\", never the list itself.\n\n## Someone else's list\n\"Sam's to-dos\": find Sam's member `id` with `list_workspace_members` (reveal it with `search_tools`), then the same call with `assignee` set to that id.",
        "views_context": null,
        "author_avatar_url": null,
        "extraction_config": {
            "actions": true,
            "decisions": true
        },
        "marketplace_category": null
    },
    {
        "id": "d15b1385-a202-4205-8e85-bf296ade857f",
        "area": "calendar",
        "icon": "🎁",
        "name": "Occasion Planner",
        "slug": "occasion",
        "color": "#ec4899",
        "model": null,
        "category": "skill",
