        "description": "A weekly customer-success digest. For each account coming up — a follow-up date approaching, or a renewal or deadline someone actually said out loud — it assembles what you owe them, what they owe you, and the questions raised on calls that were never answered. One page, per account, with receipts.",
        "forked_from": null,
        "agent_config": {
            "context_rules": [
                "No renewal-date field or contract object exists: 'approaching' means either a next_followup_at inside the window or a renewal/contract/deadline date someone actually SAID on a call and that is recorded — always say which, quote the stated ones, and never infer a renewal date from tenure or a start date.",
                "Assemble per ACCOUNT, not per person: list_contacts(relationship_type:'customer'), get_contact_details for next_followup_at (list_contacts does not return it), and get_company_overview to roll contacts up to their company.",
                "Find stated dates with find/search_claims over date language ('renewal', 'contract', 'expires', 'term ends', 'go-live', 'deadline') plus each active account name.",
                "What we owe them: list_claims(scope:'personal') plus search_claims with commitment verbs and the account name — and check the latest capture with that account (list_contact_captures → get_capture_content) before listing a commitment, so already-delivered promises never appear in a renewal brief.",
                "What they owe us: list_claims(entity_type:'contact', entity_id:<id>) per account contact (a contact's commitments hang off them by an about edge), plus a search_claims pass for unresolved speakers.",
                "Unanswered open questions are the sharpest finding: list_claims(type:'open_question') filtered to the account's contacts, company, or captures, ranked oldest-first and quoted as asked.",
                "Cap the digest at 5-8 accounts that genuinely need attention, ordered by nearest date, with unanswered questions or our own unkept promises breaking ties; name how many accounts were left out. Per account emit only the lines with content and exactly ONE move.",
