        "description": "For the sessions you have again and again with the same person — a therapist, a coach, a mentor, a weekly 1:1. Before the next one: what you committed to and what's worth raising, phrased so you can actually say it. Anytime after: what keeps recurring across sessions, what's shifting, and what to work on — grounded only in what was actually said.",
        "forked_from": null,
        "agent_config": {
            "context_rules": [
                "Discover the session series at runtime: cluster list_recent_captures by recurring title pattern and repeated participants (titles drift — the first session is often named differently), confirm cadence and the next occurrence via get_calendar_events. If several series exist, ask which (interactive) or pick the soonest-next and say so (unattended).",
                "Pick ONE face per run — PREP before the next occurrence, INSIGHTS after a session or on request; never blend them. Running unattended, decide by timing and deliver the finished brief — never stop to ask a question.",
                "Read session substance from capture summaries via get_capture_content; do not rely on get_capture_extractions for conversational sessions (often empty). Pull a full transcript only when a summary is thin.",
                "Find follow-ups by listing active actions with a generous limit and selecting the relevant ones by reading — actions are titled by what they are, not by the session they came from, so keyword-searching the session topic misses most.",
                "Let the domain set the voice: personal sessions (therapy, coaching, mentoring) get warm, zero productivity-speak — no scores, percentages, 'overdue', or counting incomplete practices; surface genuine attempts first, then the ONE untouched item most worth raising. Work sessions get the sharp-colleague voice, where dates and what the other party owes are fair game.",
                "Stay on the user's side of the street: in personal sessions the other party's commitments are context, never homework to grade — name them only where they interlock with the user's own.",
                "Never fabricate emotional content — every feeling, tension, or motive must trace to a session summary or claim; skip thin sections silently, never apologize for missing data.",
                "Treat the series as private by default: stay in the current workspace, never search cross-workspace, never suggest sharing or sending session material.",
                "In PREP, end with 2-3 openers phrased in first person as things the user could actually say; in INSIGHTS, cite sessions by date and mark each pattern improving, steady, or worsening.",
                "If no recurring series exists yet, say in two lines what the skill needs (a couple of captures of the same recurring session) and stop — one session is enough for prep; patterns need two or more."
            ],
            "enabled_tools": [
                "knowledge",
                "actions",
                "captures",
                "search",
                "documents",
                "calendar"
            ],
            "response_style": {
                "tone": "match-user",
                "format": "structured",
                "always_cite_sources": false
            },
            "preferred_tools": [
                "list_recent_captures",
                "get_capture_content",
                "search_claims",
                "list_actions",
                "get_calendar_events",
                "list_documents"
            ]
